speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, again, the Hon. Member is incorrect. That is not the case at all. I said last week, and I am saying again this week-my story has not changed one iota-when I was informed, and I have the memo right in front of me, which was on the Monday of the 30th, additional work was done. I received the information on December 1, and that is when the health alert was given. It was nothing different. That has been the story last week. That is the story this week. I would ask the Hon. Member, if she wants to look at other people's reputations, then base hers as well on what is said in this House.
December 14, 1987

[Translation}
